<!--
  All user-facing copy lives here so the app can be translated without touching Kotlin.
  `values-hi/strings.xml` is the Hindi (hi-rIN) translation; anything marked
  translatable="false" is a proper noun or a unit symbol and stays as-is.

  Formatting rules for this file:
   - Strings with placeholders use positional specifiers (%1$s, %2$d) and are always
     read through the formatting APIs (stringResource(id, arg) / getString(id, arg)).
   - A literal percent inside such a string is written %%.
   - Apostrophes are escaped (\') and ampersands are written &amp;.
-->
